    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d138-f1" n="3" type="source" xml:id="d138-f1-content">
                <p>Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d138-f2" n="4" xml:id="d138-f2-content">
                <p>Dulles approved these courses of action at the August 1 scheduled meeting; see
                        <ref target="#d139">Document 139</ref>. At the end of the first sentence
                    Dulles added a phrase so that it read: “a) Furnish token military
                    aid—particularly to the Army—totaling about $7 million on phased basis and on
                    military level so far as practicable.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
